---
layout: base
---

{#
    A project is a post that leads with a picture. The header is the post's —
    title, standfirst, meta row — and so are the prose and figure rules, so a
    project reads as part of the same site rather than a gallery bolted on.
    What differs is the cover between the header and the prose, and a meta
    row that carries the project's date and disciplines and nothing else.

    No back link and nothing after the prose, as on posts. How a page points
    back to its section is a question for the whole site, not this layout.
#}
<article class="post project">
    <header class="post-header">
        <h1 class="post-title">{{ title }}</h1>
        {%- if description %}
        <p class="post-standfirst">{{ description }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
        <div class="post-metadata project-metadata">
            <span>{{ year | projectDate(month) }}</span>
            {%- for discipline in disciplines %}
            <span class="post-metadata__separator" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
            <span>{{ discipline }}</span>
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>
    </header>
    {%- if cover %}
    <img class="project-cover" src="{{ cover }}" alt="{{ coverAlt }}" loading="eager" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 720px, 100vw">
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="post-content">
        {{ content | safe }}
    </div>
</article>
